      "body": "Beta diversity: how different the communities of two samples are. The PCoA places each sample so that the closer two points sit, the more alike their communities, and the Bray-Curtis matrix beside it holds the distances it was drawn from. When the run tested it, PERMANOVA says how much of that variation the grouping explains.\n",
